{%- doc -%}
  KONBINI overrides for the product card — ticket 11.

  The card is the photograph, the title and the price, plus the quick-add
  icon that `konbini-quick-add-styles` draws. Values come from the resolved
  ticket and its specimen (`Wayfinder/assets/11-product-card-build.py`):

  - Photograph: 1:1 on a tint-25 tile, multiplied onto it. The tile is also
    the no-image state.
  - Title: the full catalogue title (decision D9), 13px, Medium, tint-900.
    Up to three lines on narrow screens, where two lines would cut the size
    off the end. Untruncated from 750px up.
  - Price: 13px, Bold, tint-950, tabular figures.
  - The price is pushed to the foot of the card, so every price in a grid row
    lands on one line at whatever height that row's longest title needs.
  - Line height and breaking follow the language (ticket 30).

  Not here yet: the size-keeping cut and row alignment (needs a script), the
  sold-out wording, and the chip mode.

  Tint values are written out until ticket 41 delivers tokens from Figma.
  Selectors repeat `.product-card` to outrank Horizon without depending on
  stylesheet order. Horizon's snippets stay untouched.

  @example
  {% render 'konbini-product-card-styles' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .product-card.product-card {
    --konbini-tint-25: #fafafa;
    --konbini-tint-900: #373737;
    --konbini-tint-950: #232323;
  }

  /* The card owns its own vertical rhythm: 10px under the photograph, 9px
     above the price. Horizon's uniform gap would add to both. */
  .product-card.product-card .product-card__content {
    /* Set as a property: Horizon writes the gap variable inline, which a
       stylesheet cannot outrank. */
    gap: 0;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .card-gallery {
    background: var(--konbini-tint-25);
  }

  .product-card.product-card .card-gallery img {
    mix-blend-mode: multiply;
  }

  /* No photograph: the bare tile is the state (ticket 01). Horizon prints the
     title inside it in display type; the title already sits under the tile. */
  .product-card.product-card .product-card-gallery__title-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    padding: 0;
    background: var(--konbini-tint-25);
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .product-card-gallery__title-placeholder .title-text {
    display: none;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .product-card__content > a.contents > .text-block {
    width: 100%;
    padding-block-start: 0;
    max-width: none;
    margin-block-start: 10px;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .product-card__content > a.contents > .text-block p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--konbini-tint-900);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.45;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .product-card__content > a.contents > .text-block p:lang(ja) {
    line-height: 1.75;
    line-break: strict;
  }

  .product-card.product-card .product-card__content > a.contents > .text-block p:lang(ko) {
    line-height: 1.6;
    word-break: keep-all;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .product-card.product-card .product-card__content > a.contents > .text-block p {
      display: -webkit-box;
      overflow: hidden;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
      line-clamp: 3;
    }
  }

  .product-card.product-card product-price {
    margin-block-start: auto;
    padding-block-start: 9px;
  }

  .product-card.product-card product-price .price {
    color: var(--konbini-tint-950);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
